@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="narrow mx-auto">
    <h1 class="h2 fw-bold mb-4">Privacy</h1>

    <p>GarageDesk is a workshop manager that is still under development. This page explains, in plain terms, what it stores.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">What we store</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Your account: your email address and a securely hashed password (we never store the password itself).</li>
        <li>Your shop's details and, as the app grows, the customers, vehicles and jobs you enter.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Who can see it</h2>
    <p>Each shop is separate. Signed-in users only ever see their own shop's data.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Cookies</h2>
    <p>A single sign-in cookie keeps you logged in. There is no advertising or tracking.</p>
</div>
